    content: "# MASTER PROJECT PROMPT \342\200\224 PRINTREADY\n## Complete Document Wallet, Smart Printing, Print Shop Marketplace & Business Ecosystem\n\nYou are an elite product development team consisting of a senior software architect, Flutter developer, frontend engineer, backend engineer, UI/UX designer, AI engineer, cybersecurity specialist, QA engineer, DevOps engineer, and product manager.\n\nYour task is to design, develop, test, and deliver a complete, production-oriented application ecosystem called **PrintReady**.\n\nDo not build a simple prototype, static mockup, landing page, or UI-only demonstration.\n\nBuild a real, functional, full-stack product with connected frontend, backend, database, authentication, secure file storage, APIs, integrations, error handling, and deployment infrastructure.\n\n---\n\n# 1. PRODUCT VISION\n\nPrintReady is an all-in-one document wallet and digital printing ecosystem.\n\nUsers should be able to upload documents in advance, securely store them, organize them, scan new documents, search them, edit supported document formats, configure printing preferences, save printing shops, and send files instantly through WhatsApp, email, or the integrated PrintReady printing marketplace.\n\nCustomers should be able to discover nearby printing shops, place orders, receive pricing, pay digitally, track printing progress, chat with shops, and collect or receive printed documents.\n\nPrinting businesses should have their own business management platform for receiving orders, managing customers, pricing, printing queues, staff, payments, inventory, delivery, promotions, reviews, and analytics.\n\nAdministrators should have a complete platform management dashboard.\n\nThe product should eventually support Android, iOS, web, and desktop-compatible architecture where practical.\n\n## Core slogan\n\n**Upload once. Print anywhere.**\n\n## Core user problem\n\nUsers often need to print documents urgently but must find the files on their phone, download them, send them to a shop, explain print settings, and repeat this process every time.\n\nPrintReady eliminates unnecessary steps by keeping documents ready and allowing users to send them to a print shop in seconds.\n\n---\n\n# 2. DEVELOPMENT RULES\n\nFollow these rules throughout development.\n\n1. Build a real working application.\n2. Do not create fake buttons or nonfunctional screens.\n3. Do not simulate successful uploads, payments, orders, authentication, or integrations.\n4. Do not use hardcoded fake data in production functionality.\n5. Use realistic mock data only in clearly labeled development/demo mode.\n6. Every interactive element must have a working action.\n7. Every feature must have its own functional implementation or a clearly documented integration requirement.\n8. Maintain a feature checklist.\n9. Do not silently omit features.\n10. Do not replace requested features with simplified alternatives without documenting the limitation.\n11. Build in development milestones, but maintain the complete product scope from the beginning.\n12. Maintain architectural consistency across customer app, shop app, web portal, and admin dashboard.\n13. Prioritize Android as the primary mobile platform initially.\n14. Design the architecture to support future iOS and web deployment.\n15. Follow secure development practices.\n16. Never expose API secrets, private keys, payment credentials, or server secrets in frontend code.\n17. Never claim an integration is functional if credentials or approvals are missing.\n18. If an external integration requires credentials, create its integration layer, configuration, setup documentation, and testing framework.\n19. Handle errors gracefully.\n20. Preserve existing working features when adding new functionality.\n21. Do not rewrite stable components unnecessarily.\n22. Use modular, maintainable, reusable code.\n23. Write documentation alongside development.\n24. Use automated testing wherever possible.\n25. Before marking a feature complete, test its complete workflow.\n\n---\n\n# 3. PRODUCT ECOSYSTEM\n\nBuild four connected products.\n\n## Product A: Customer Mobile App\n\nPrimary users:\n\n- Students\n- College students\n- Office workers\n- Job seekers\n- Business owners\n- Individuals\n- Anyone needing document printing\n\nThe customer app must contain:\n\n- Account and profile management\n- Secure document vault\n- Document uploads\n- Folders\n- File search\n- AI document organization\n- Document scanner\n- OCR\n- PDF tools\n- Print basket\n- Printing presets\n- Print preview\n- Printing shop discovery\n- Shop profiles\n- Saved shops\n- Instant WhatsApp sharing\n- Email sharing\n- Native file sharing\n- Marketplace orders\n- Payments\n- Order tracking\n- Chat\n- Pickup and delivery\n- Reviews\n- Coupons\n- Loyalty rewards\n- Notifications\n- Cloud backup\n- Multi-device sync\n- Security settings\n- Subscription management\n- Help and support\n\n## Product B: Printing Shop App\n\nPrinting businesses need:\n\n- Shop registration\n- Business verification\n- Shop profile\n- Services\n- Pricing\n- Incoming orders\n- File downloads\n- Print queue\n- Order management\n- Customer communication\n- Price confirmation\n- Payments\n- Receipts\n- Pickup\n- Delivery\n- Staff management\n- Printer management\n- Inventory\n- Promotions\n- Coupons\n- Analytics\n- Reports\n- Reviews\n- Notifications\n- Business settings\n\n## Product C: Web Platform\n\nBuild a responsive web platform supporting:\n\n- Customer web access\n- Document uploads\n- Document management\n- Online printing orders\n- Shop discovery\n- Shop owner dashboard\n- Order management\n- Chat\n- Pricing\n- Analytics\n- Account management\n\n## Product D: Admin Dashboard\n\nBuild a secured administrative web dashboard for:\n\n- Users\n- Shops\n- Verification\n- Orders\n- Payments\n- Refunds\n- Complaints\n- Reviews\n- Support\n- Subscriptions\n- Promotions\n- Platform settings\n- Analytics\n- Security\n- Audit logs\n\n---\n\n# 4. TECHNOLOGY STACK\n\nUse the following recommended architecture unless a strong technical reason requires a change.\n\n## Mobile\n\n- Flutter\n- Dart\n- Material 3 design system\n- Riverpod or another scalable state-management solution\n- GoRouter for navigation\n- Modular feature architecture\n- Local persistent database\n- Secure storage\n- Native Android integrations\n\n## Backend\n\n- Firebase Authentication\n- Cloud Firestore\n- Firebase Storage or secure compatible object storage\n- Cloud Functions\n- Firebase Cloud Messaging\n- Firebase App Check\n- Firebase Crashlytics\n- Firebase Analytics\n- Firebase Remote Config\n\n## Web\n\n- Next.js\n- TypeScript\n- Responsive design\n- Reusable components\n- Secure authentication\n- API-driven architecture\n\n## AI\n\n- Gemini API through secure backend\n- Google ML Kit for on-device OCR where appropriate\n- AI document classification\n- AI search\n- AI-assisted print configuration\n- AI assistant\n\n## Maps\n\n- Google Maps integration\n- Places search if properly configured\n- Geolocation permission handling\n- Map and list views\n\n## Payments\n\nDesign a payment-provider abstraction.\n\nFor India, support integration with an appropriate provider such as Razorpay, subject to merchant onboarding, credentials, and applicable requirements.\n\nSupport:\n\n- UPI\n- QR\n- Cards where supported\n- Payment status verification\n- Refunds\n- Webhooks\n- Transaction reconciliation\n\nNever treat a client-side payment success screen as proof of payment.\n\n## Email\n\nUse a secure backend email service.\n\nSupport:\n\n- Email verification\n- Transactional email\n- Order receipts\n- Order notifications\n- Password/account recovery\n- Support communication\n\n## WhatsApp\n\nImplement supported WhatsApp sharing functionality.\n\nSupport:\n\n- WhatsApp\n- WhatsApp Business where installed\n- Prepared text messages\n- File attachments through native sharing\n- Saved shop contact details\n- Direct contact initiation\n\nWhere official WhatsApp Business APIs are appropriate, create a separate integration layer.\n\nDo not assume that ordinary WhatsApp allows automatically sending arbitrary files to a chosen recipient without the user confirming the send.\n\n## Architecture\n\nUse a modular architecture.\n\nOrganize code into:\n\n- Presentation layer\n- Application/state layer\n- Domain layer\n- Data layer\n- Backend/API layer\n- Integration layer\n- Security layer\n\nSeparate customer, shop, and admin permissions.\n\nUse reusable components and shared business logic wherever appropriate.\n\n---\n\n# 5. BRANDING AND DESIGN SYSTEM\n\nCreate a polished, premium, modern application.\n\nThe design should feel:\n\n- Professional\n- Simple\n- Fast\n- Trustworthy\n- Modern\n- Organized\n- Accessible\n- Premium\n- Friendly without being childish\n\n## Visual direction\n\nUse a clean productivity-app design.\n\nRecommended visual palette:\n\n- Primary: Deep indigo or dark blue\n- Secondary: Vibrant violet or blue\n- Accent: Teal or green for successful actions\n- Background: Neutral light grey/white\n- Dark mode: Deep charcoal backgrounds\n- Cards: Rounded corners, subtle borders\n- Typography: Modern readable sans-serif\n\nUse consistent:\n\n- Spacing\n- Typography\n- Buttons\n- Icons\n- Cards\n- Inputs\n- Dialogs\n- Bottom sheets\n- Navigation\n- Loading indicators\n- Error states\n- Empty states\n- Confirmation states\n\nAvoid:\n\n- Excessive gradients\n- Excessive animations\n- Clutter\n- Tiny text\n- Unnecessary decorations\n- Fake dashboard statistics\n- Unnecessary onboarding screens\n- Buttons without functionality\n\n## Accessibility\n\nSupport:\n\n- Readable text\n- Large text\n- Screen reader labels\n- Keyboard navigation on web\n- High contrast\n- Accessible touch targets\n- Meaningful error messages\n\n---\n\n# 6. AUTHENTICATION AND ACCOUNT MANAGEMENT\n\nImplement:\n\n- Email signup\n- Email login\n- Phone signup\n- Phone OTP verification\n- Google authentication\n- Password recovery\n- Email verification\n- Phone verification\n- Profile management\n- Profile picture\n- Name\n- Phone\n- Email\n- Addresses\n- Preferred language\n- Theme\n- Notification settings\n- Security settings\n\nSupport account roles:\n\n- Customer\n- Shop owner\n- Shop employee\n- Admin\n- Support agent\n\nImplement secure role-based access control.\n\nUsers must not be able to grant themselves admin or shop-owner privileges by modifying client-side data.\n\nImplement:\n\n- Session management\n- Logout\n- Logout from all devices\n- Device list\n- Account deletion\n- Account data export\n- Authentication rate limits\n- Abuse prevention\n- Secure recovery workflows\n\n---\n\n# 7. DOCUMENT VAULT\n\nCreate a full document management system.\n\n## File types\n\nSupport storage and appropriate preview for:\n\n- PDF\n- JPG\n- JPEG\n- PNG\n- WebP\n- HEIC where supported\n- DOC\n- DOCX\n- XLS\n- XLSX\n- PPT\n- PPTX\n- TXT\n\nOther file types may be stored with limited preview support where appropriate.\n\n## Upload\n\nSupport:\n\n- Single upload\n- Multiple uploads\n- Drag and drop on web\n- File picker\n- Camera import\n- Gallery import\n- Device storage\n- Cloud import when integrated\n- Upload progress\n- Retry\n- Cancellation\n- Resume where technically supported\n- Upload queue\n\n## File management\n\nImplement:\n\n- Rename\n- Move\n- Copy\n- Delete\n- Restore\n- Permanently delete\n- Favourite\n- Share\n- Download\n- Preview\n- Duplicate detection\n- Tags\n- Version history\n- Metadata\n- File size\n- Creation date\n- Last modified date\n\n## Folders\n\nSupport:\n\n- Custom folders\n- Nested folders\n- Categories\n- Folder colours/icons\n- Folder search\n- Folder sorting\n- Batch actions\n\nSuggested categories:\n\n- Identity\n- Education\n- College\n- Job\n- Resume\n- Certificates\n- Banking\n- Government\n- Travel\n- Medical\n- Personal\n- Photos\n- Business\n- Other\n\nUsers must be able to create their own categories.\n\n## Search\n\nSearch by:\n\n- Filename\n- Folder\n- Category\n- Tags\n- File type\n- Date\n- OCR content\n- Document metadata\n\nImplement filters.\n\n## Recent files\n\nDisplay:\n\n- Recently uploaded\n- Recently opened\n- Recently printed\n- Recently shared\n\n## Favourites\n\nUsers can favourite:\n\n- Documents\n- Folders\n- Shops\n- Print presets\n\n## Trash\n\nImplement:\n\n- Recover deleted documents\n- Permanent deletion\n- Automatic trash cleanup based on configurable retention\n- Confirmation before permanent deletion\n\n## Local and cloud storage\n\nSupport:\n\n- Local storage\n- Optional cloud backup\n- Cloud sync\n- Multi-device sync\n- Offline access\n- Storage usage display\n- Backup status\n- Sync status\n- Conflict handling\n\nNever expose cloud files publicly.\n\n---\n\n# 8. AI DOCUMENT INTELLIGENCE\n\nCreate a secure AI-powered document system.\n\n## AI classification\n\nAutomatically detect document types:\n\n- Resume\n- ID card\n- Certificate\n- Application\n- Invoice\n- Receipt\n- Ticket\n- Photo\n- Notes\n- Letter\n- Contract\n- Other\n\nAI should suggest:\n\n- Document title\n- Category\n- Folder\n- Tags\n- Relevant date\n- Expiration date where applicable\n\nThe user must be able to approve, edit, or reject suggestions.\n\n## OCR\n\nImplement OCR for:\n\n- Scanned PDFs\n- Images\n- Camera scans\n\nExtract text for searchable indexing.\n\n## AI search\n\nAllow natural-language queries such as:\n\n- Find my college ID.\n- Show my resume.\n- Find my bank document.\n- Find the certificate containing my name.\n- Show files uploaded last week.\n- Find my latest resume.\n\n## Document summarization\n\nAllow users to summarize documents.\n\n## Duplicate detection\n\nDetect:\n\n- Exact duplicates\n- Similar documents\n- Different versions of the same document\n\nProvide a review interface.\n\n## Expiry reminders\n\nAllow reminders for documents such as:\n\n- Passport\n- Certificates\n- ID cards\n- Licenses\n- Other user-selected documents\n\nUsers must control reminder dates and notifications.\n\n## Privacy\n\nAI processing must:\n\n- Use a secure backend\n- Avoid exposing API keys\n- Respect user consent\n- Avoid unnecessary retention\n- Explain processing where sensitive files are involved\n- Allow disabling AI features\n\n---\n\n# 9. DOCUMENT SCANNER\n\nBuild a full scanning experience.\n\n## Camera scanner\n\nImplement:\n\n- Camera capture\n- Document edge detection\n- Auto capture where supported\n- Manual capture\n- Crop\n- Perspective correction\n- Rotate\n- Brightness\n- Contrast\n- Filters\n- Grayscale\n- Black and white\n- Colour\n- Shadow removal where supported\n\n## Multi-page scanning\n\nSupport:\n\n- Multiple pages\n- Page reorder\n- Page deletion\n- Page replacement\n- Page preview\n- Add pages later\n- Combine pages\n\n## Export\n\nExport scanned documents as:\n\n- PDF\n- JPG\n- PNG\n\nSupport:\n\n- OCR\n- Searchable PDF where possible\n- Compression\n- Filename\n- Category\n- Folder selection\n\n## Document utilities\n\nImplement:\n\n- PDF merge\n- PDF split\n- PDF compress\n- PDF rotate\n- Page reorder\n- PDF page deletion\n- Image to PDF\n- PDF to image\n- Add watermark\n- PDF password protection\n- PDF page numbering\n- Resize images\n- Image compression\n- Image crop\n- Supported format conversion\n\nOnly implement password removal for files the user is authorized to access.\n\n---\n\n# 10. PRINT BASKET\n\nCreate a dedicated print basket.\n\nUsers can:\n\n- Select multiple documents\n- Add documents to basket\n- Remove documents\n- Change order\n- View selected files\n- Set individual printing options\n- Set shared printing options\n- Save the basket\n- Reuse previous baskets\n- Create print collections\n\n## Per-document settings\n\nImplement:\n\n- Copies\n- Paper size\n- Colour\n- Black & white\n- Single-sided\n- Double-sided\n- Orientation\n- Page range\n- Scaling\n- Fit to page\n- Actual size\n- Custom scaling\n- Paper type\n- Layout\n- Pages per sheet\n- Collation\n- Binding\n- Stapling\n- Special instructions\n\n## Paper sizes\n\nSupport:\n\n- A4\n- A3\n- A5\n- Letter\n- Legal\n- Custom\n\n## Page range\n\nSupport:\n\n- All pages\n- Specific pages\n- Ranges\n- Multiple ranges\n\nExample:\n\n1-5, 8, 10-12\n\nValidate page ranges.\n\n## Copies\n\nAllow individual copy counts per document.\n\n## Print presets\n\nUsers can create, edit, delete, and save unlimited presets.\n\nExamples:\n\n- College\n- Office\n- Resume\n- Certificate\n- Notes\n- ID\n- Photo\n- Legal\n- Custom\n\nA preset can contain:\n\n- Paper size\n- Colour\n- Sides\n- Orientation\n- Copies\n- Layout\n- Scaling\n- Paper type\n- Binding\n\nAllow applying a preset to multiple documents.\n\n---\n\n# 11. PRINT PREVIEW\n\nBefore sending a print job:\n\n- Preview PDF\n- Preview images\n- Preview page selection\n- Preview orientation\n- Preview paper size\n- Preview scaling\n- Preview copies\n- Preview colour settings\n- Display page count\n- Display estimated sheets\n- Detect unsupported files\n- Warn about large files\n- Warn about low-resolution images\n- Warn about blank pages where possible\n- Warn about potentially cropped content\n\nImplement print cost estimation.\n\nDo not claim to accurately simulate printer output where the actual printer characteristics are unknown.\n\n---\n\n# 12. PRINT COST CALCULATOR\n\nSupport pricing for:\n\n- B&W pages\n- Colour pages\n- A4\n- A3\n- A5\n- Letter\n- Legal\n- Photo prints\n- Premium paper\n- Binding\n- Lamination\n- Scanning\n- Photocopying\n- ID printing\n- Other services\n\nAllow shop-specific pricing.\n\nCalculate:\n\n- Per-document cost\n- Total copies\n- Estimated pages\n- Estimated sheets\n- Subtotal\n- Discounts\n- Service charges\n- Delivery\n- Tax where applicable\n- Total\n\nDisplay price as an estimate until confirmed by the shop.\n\n---\n\n# 13. SAVED PRINTING SHOPS\n\nCreate a dedicated shop directory.\n\nUsers should be able to save printing shops even if those shops are not registered on PrintReady.\n\n## Shop information\n\nStore:\n\n- Shop name\n- Owner name if known\n- Phone\n- WhatsApp\n- WhatsApp Business number\n- Email\n- Address\n- Location coordinates\n- Google Maps link\n- Opening hours\n- Notes\n- Services\n- Pricing\n- Preferred contact method\n- Shop photo\n- Website\n- Social links\n\n## Saved shops\n\nImplement:\n\n- Favourite shops\n- Default shop\n- Shop groups\n- Shop notes\n- Shop-specific preferences\n- Contact\n- Call\n- WhatsApp\n- Email\n- Directions\n- Previous orders\n\n## Shop groups\n\nAllow custom groups such as:\n\n- Near home\n- College\n- Office\n- Trusted\n- Cheapest\n- Favourite\n\n## Shop-specific presets\n\nRemember settings per shop.\n\nExample:\n\nShop A:\n\n- A4\n- B&W\n- Double-sided\n- WhatsApp\n\nShop B:\n\n- Colour\n- Single-sided\n- Email\n\nAllow users to edit and override preferences.\n\n---\n\n# 14. SHOP DISCOVERY\n\nImplement:\n\n- Nearby shops\n- Search\n- Map\n- List\n- Distance\n- Ratings\n- Reviews\n- Open/closed status\n- Services\n- Pricing\n- Delivery\n- Pickup\n- Online ordering\n- Filters\n- Sort\n\nFilters:\n\n- Distance\n- Rating\n- Price\n- Service\n- Open now\n- Pickup\n- Delivery\n- Verified\n- Online ordering\n\nLocation access must be optional.\n\nUsers can manually enter a location if they deny GPS access.\n\n---\n\n# 15. SHOP PROFILE\n\nEvery registered shop needs:\n\n- Name\n- Logo\n- Photos\n- Owner\n- Address\n- Map location\n- Phone\n- WhatsApp\n- Email\n- Opening hours\n- Holiday hours\n- Services\n- Price list\n- Paper types\n- Printing options\n- Payment methods\n- Pickup\n- Delivery\n- Estimated turnaround time\n- Rating\n- Reviews\n- Verification status\n- Contact buttons\n\nAllow shops to update profiles.\n\n---\n\n# 16. DIRECT SHARING\n\nImplement native sharing for Android and supported platforms.\n\n## WhatsApp\n\nAllow:\n\n- Select files\n- Select shop contact\n- Prepare message\n- Share files\n- Open WhatsApp\n- WhatsApp Business\n- Send instructions\n- Share multiple documents where supported\n\nThe user may need to select the destination conversation and confirm sending.\n\nDo not claim that normal WhatsApp supports silent automatic file delivery.\n\n## Email\n\nPrepare:\n\n- Recipient\n- CC where requested\n- Subject\n- Message\n- Selected attachments\n- Print settings\n\nOpen a supported email composer.\n\n## Native share sheet\n\nSupport:\n\n- Bluetooth\n- Nearby Share\n- WhatsApp\n- Email\n- Other compatible apps\n\nHandle large files and sharing errors.\n\n## Message templates\n\nAllow:\n\n- Default template\n- Shop-specific template\n- Custom template\n- Template variables\n\nVariables:\n\n- Customer name\n- Shop name\n- Document names\n- Copies\n- Settings\n- Pickup time\n- Order number\n\nExample:\n\n\"Hello, please print the attached files. Settings: {{settings}}. Copies: {{copies}}. Please let me know the total price and estimated completion time.\"\n\n---\n\n# 17. PRINTREADY MARKETPLACE ORDERS\n\nRegistered shops can receive digital printing orders directly.\n\n## Order creation\n\nCustomer selects:\n\n- Shop\n- Documents\n- Print settings\n- Copies\n- Pickup or delivery\n- Preferred time\n- Special instructions\n\nSystem creates:\n\n- Unique order number\n- Order summary\n- File references\n- Price estimate\n- Order status\n- Customer information\n\n## Shop response\n\nShop can:\n\n- Accept\n- Reject\n- Request clarification\n- Modify estimated price\n- Confirm availability\n- Confirm turnaround time\n\nAny price change must be shown to the customer for approval.\n\n## Customer approval\n\nCustomer can:\n\n- Approve price\n- Reject price\n- Cancel\n- Ask questions\n- Pay\n\n## Order statuses\n\nImplement:\n\n- Draft\n- Submitted\n- Received\n- Awaiting shop response\n- Accepted\n- Rejected\n- Price pending approval\n- Approved\n- Payment pending\n- Paid\n- Printing\n- Quality check\n- Ready for pickup\n- Out for delivery\n- Delivered\n- Completed\n- Cancelled\n- Refund requested\n- Refunded\n\nImplement a status transition system.\n\nPrevent invalid transitions.\n\nRecord timestamps and actors.\n\n---\n\n# 18. PRINT SHOP APPLICATION\n\nCreate a shop-owner interface.\n\n## Onboarding\n\n- Create account\n- Register shop\n- Verify phone\n- Verify email\n- Business details\n- Shop address\n- GPS location\n- Upload photos\n- Add services\n- Set prices\n- Set operating hours\n- Set pickup/delivery\n- Verification process\n\n## Dashboard\n\nShow actual business statistics:\n\n- New orders\n- Pending orders\n- Printing\n- Ready\n- Completed today\n- Revenue today\n- Revenue this month\n- Outstanding payments\n- Order volume\n\nOnly display real data.\n\n## Order management\n\nImplement:\n\n- New orders\n- Accept/reject\n- Customer details\n- Document list\n- Secure file access\n- Print instructions\n- Price\n- Status\n- Priority\n- Due time\n- Staff assignment\n- Download\n- Print queue\n- Completion\n- Pickup\n- Delivery\n\n## Print queue\n\nShop can:\n\n- Sort by priority\n- Sort by deadline\n- Group jobs\n- Filter\n- View file details\n- Download files\n- View print specifications\n- Track progress\n- Assign staff\n\n## Customer management\n\nImplement:\n\n- Customer profiles\n- Order history\n- Preferences\n- Contact information\n- Notes\n- Loyalty\n- Search\n\n## Pricing\n\nCreate editable price lists.\n\nPrices may depend on:\n\n- Paper size\n- Colour\n- Sides\n- Copies\n- Paper quality\n- Service\n- Binding\n- Lamination\n- Special work\n\n## Shop staff\n\nSupport:\n\n- Staff invitations\n- Role assignment\n- Permissions\n- Staff accounts\n- Activity records\n\nRoles:\n\n- Owner\n- Manager\n- Printer/operator\n- Cashier\n- Delivery staff\n\n---\n\n# 19. SHOP INVENTORY AND EQUIPMENT\n\nImplement shop inventory management.\n\nTrack:\n\n- Paper\n- Ink\n- Toner\n- Photo paper\n- Binding materials\n- Lamination sheets\n- Other supplies\n\nFeatures:\n\n- Stock levels\n- Low-stock warnings\n- Purchase entries\n- Usage\n- Inventory history\n- Supplier details\n\nPrinter management:\n\n- Printer name\n- Printer type\n- Supported sizes\n- Colour support\n- Duplex\n- Status\n- Maintenance records\n- Assigned jobs\n\nDo not attempt direct printer control unless the printer and platform support it.\n\n---\n\n# 20. PAYMENT SYSTEM\n\nCreate a secure payment abstraction.\n\nSupport provider integration.\n\n## Payment options\n\n- UPI\n- QR\n- Cash\n- Cards\n- Supported online payment methods\n\n## Payment workflow\n\n1. Shop confirms order.\n2. Customer receives final price.\n3. Customer approves.\n4. Customer chooses payment.\n5. Payment gateway processes.\n6. Backend verifies transaction.\n7. Order payment status updates.\n8. Shop receives confirmation.\n\n## Payment functionality\n\n- Payment initiation\n- Payment verification\n- Webhooks\n- Transaction IDs\n- Receipts\n- Refunds\n- Refund status\n- Failed payment handling\n- Reconciliation\n\n## Important\n\n- Never store raw card details.\n- Never trust client payment status.\n- Validate payment on backend.\n- Use idempotency where supported.\n- Verify webhook signatures.\n- Prevent duplicate payment processing.\n- Maintain transaction audit logs.\n\n---\n\n# 21. PICKUP AND DELIVERY\n\n## Pickup\n\nSupport:\n\n- Pickup time\n- Pickup instructions\n- Ready notification\n- QR code\n- Order number\n- Collection verification\n\n## Delivery\n\nSupport:\n\n- Address book\n- Delivery address\n- Delivery fee\n- Delivery instructions\n- Tracking\n- Delivery status\n- Shop delivery\n- Courier integration where available\n- Delivery confirmation\n\nDelivery options depend on shop capability.\n\n---\n\n# 22. CHAT SYSTEM\n\nCreate order-based chat.\n\nCustomer and shop can communicate.\n\nFeatures:\n\n- Text\n- File attachments\n- Images\n- Order reference\n- Quick replies\n- Price clarification\n- Print clarification\n- Pickup instructions\n- Delivery instructions\n- Message timestamps\n- Read status\n- Notifications\n\nExample quick replies for shops:\n\n- Order received\n- Price confirmed\n- Please clarify print settings\n- File is unreadable\n- Printing started\n- Ready for pickup\n- Please collect before closing\n\nUse secure access controls.\n\n---\n\n# 23. NOTIFICATIONS\n\nImplement in-app and push notifications.\n\nCustomer:\n\n- Upload success\n- Backup\n- Sync\n- New order\n- Shop accepted\n- Price change\n- Payment\n- Printing\n- Ready\n- Delivery\n- Completion\n- Refund\n- Chat\n- Reminder\n- Expiration\n\nShop:\n\n- New order\n- Customer approval\n- Payment\n- Cancellation\n- Chat\n- Pickup\n- Delivery\n- Review\n- Low inventory\n\nAdmin:\n\n- Reports\n- Fraud alerts\n- Payment issues\n- Shop verification\n- Complaints\n- System health\n\nAllow notification preferences.\n\n---\n\n# 24. REVIEWS AND TRUST\n\nImplement:\n\n- Ratings\n- Written reviews\n- Verified-order badges\n- Shop responses\n- Review moderation\n- Review reporting\n- Shop reporting\n- Customer complaint workflow\n- Verification badges\n\nAllow reviews only after valid orders for verified-purchase status.\n\n---\n\n# 25. LOYALTY AND PROMOTIONS\n\nImplement:\n\n- Loyalty points\n- Rewards\n- Coupons\n- Referral system\n- Shop discounts\n- Platform discounts\n- Promotional campaigns\n- Customer levels\n- Repeat customer rewards\n- Coupon validation\n\nMake all promotional rules configurable.\n\nPrevent abuse.\n\n---\n\n# 26. ADMIN DASHBOARD\n\nBuild a full admin web portal.\n\n## Dashboard\n\nShow:\n\n- Total users\n- Active users\n- New users\n- Registered shops\n- Verified shops\n- Total orders\n- Pending orders\n- Completed orders\n- Failed orders\n- Revenue\n- Payment volume\n- Refunds\n- Support tickets"
