  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Print**\n\nI\'ve successfully provisioned Firebase! I\'ve created the `firebase-applet-config.json` with the project ID and Firestore database ID, as you can see, which is a great start. Now, I\'m carefully considering how to design the print functionality and how it should interact with the rest of the application.\n\n\n**Defining the Core**\n\nI\'ve outlined the full-stack web ecosystem, detailing all its components. The focus now is on thorough planning. I\'m prioritizing the verification plan, particularly unit tests using `node:test`. I am also now creating visual assets, architecture specifications, and dependencies.\n\n\n**Testing the System**\n\nI\'m deep in the unit testing phase now, specifically focusing on the print calculator and order state machine. I\'m building tests for page range parsing, sheet calculations, and shop-specific pricing models. I\'m also testing all valid and invalid transitions in the order lifecycle, ensuring proper actor permissions and terminal state immutability. File validation, including MIME type and size limit tests, are also underway.\n\n\n**Verifying User Journeys**\n\nI\'m now focused on verifying key user journeys, specifically the Customer Document Vault, Basket, and Quick Send flow using `playwright-cli`. I\'m starting with a desktop environment (1440x900) in Demo Workspace mode. I\'m verifying the functionality of the home dashboard, and then testing the document vault, including file upload, favouriting, moving, deleting, and restoring files. Then, I will add these documents to the Print Basket and configure the print settings.\n\n\n**Validating End-to-End Flow**\n\nI\'m now integrating Print Basket interactions into the user journeys I\'m verifying. I\'m focusing on key interactions like applying presets and inspecting the print preview and cost estimate. Next, I need to check the Direct Share modal and submitting a Marketplace Order.\n\n\n**Validating Key Portals**\n\nI\'m now switching gears to the Admin Portal, and will thoroughly verify the Shop Verification queue, including approving and suspending shops. I\'ll also be inspecting Orders, Users, Audit Logs, and Platform Settings. Furthermore, I\'ll validate the Light / Dark theme toggle, ensuring crisp contrast in both modes. Finally, I will test the layout and navigation in a mobile viewport (390x844).\n\n\n**Validating Platforms**\n\nI\'m now diving into platform administration and verification. I\'ll thoroughly inspect the management of orders, disputes, payments, and refunds. I\'m also planning to review Platform Settings, promotions, and audit logs.\n\n\n**Defining Typography**\n\nI\'ve specified a 2+1 font rule. Display and Headings will use `Plus Jakarta Sans`, Body and Dense Tables are assigned `DM Sans`, while Data, Pricing, Order Numbers, and Tabular Figures will utilize `JetBrains Mono`, all loaded from Google Fonts. I\'m focusing on consistency. Also, I\'ve outlined Anti-Slop Compliance, with precise design choices in mind.\n\n\n**Integrating Dependencies**\n\nI\'m now integrating several critical dependencies within a single installation call, which includes client-side Firebase Auth, Cloud Firestore, `pdf-lib` for client-side PDF manipulation, `recharts` for analytics, and the latest `@google/genai` library for the Gemini API. Concurrently, I\'m initiating the generation of high-fidelity visual assets for featured print shops to ensure no broken image assets, as I inventory image slots for `shop_campus_press` and `shop_metro_print`.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "Kb7-ap6rN5LgkdUP1JaE-Qc"
