  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Celebrating Real Browser Verifications**\n\nI\'m incredibly excited! I just realized how valuable real browser verification is. The screenshots are crystal-clear, and we\'ve caught four significant, real-world defects that would have easily been missed otherwise. This is a huge win!\n\n\n**Refining Defect Assessments**\n\nI\'m now diving into a round one defect critique. I identified two bugs: a backend 502 error when AI OCR indexing fails, which needs a graceful fallback to local processing, and a horizontal clipping issue in the document vault table. My next step is inspecting the relevant code sections for root cause analysis.\n\n\n**Addressing UI Clippings**\n\nMy focus is now on the document vault UI. I\'ve pinpointed an overflow issue with the Actions column in the table, the star icon is clipped, and the trash icon is invisible in some viewports. I plan to use `max-w-[260px]` or `table-fixed` widths for the document filename column, to fix this issue. I\'m also addressing the cell padding to ensure all icons fit comfortably.\n\n\n**Verifying Roundtrip Shop Order**\n\nI\'m now focused on verifying a full payment roundtrip in the shop order process. The \"Accept & Send Price Confirmation\" button text is correct and explicit, but I need to include clicking it. Round 2 requires me to click \"Accept & Send Price Confirmation,\" switch to the customer view, \"Approve Price & Pay,\" then verify the HMAC roundtrip\'s success. After that, I will advance the process to the end, and verify the shop\'s dashboard revenue. I also found a UI truncation issue in the shop sidebar and spacing inconsistencies on the home page.\n\n\n**Improving Text Legibility**\n\nI\'m now focusing on text legibility improvements. In particular, I am cleaning up text labels in `Team & Reviews`, and ensuring that there are no ellipsis. I also need to make sure the text snapshots and screen readers can read a label cleanly. In addition, I am going to verify all of the phenomenal work that has been completed: the customer home, the print shops directory, the scanner and PDF tools, as well as several other elements. All have great typography and spacing.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "Qcf-aqKyB7WjvdIP7aLPgAw"
