  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Table Overflow**\n\nOkay, I\'ve zoomed in on `DocumentVaultView.tsx`, specifically lines 669-755. The `<table>`\'s dynamic width, coupled with the first cell\'s `max-w-xs sm:max-w-sm` and `whitespace-nowrap`, plus those five action icons, looks like the culprit. I\'m focusing on how these elements interact to cause the overflow.\n\n\n**Fixing Table Width Issues**\n\nI\'ve got the table fixed! By assigning it `table-fixed w-full` on desktop, with specified column widths, I\'ve eliminated the overflow. This ensures clean truncation of filenames, tags, and even those action icons. I\'m especially happy with how the actions column, at `w-[18%]`, cleanly accommodates all five icons. I\'ve also implemented fallback mechanisms for the AI routes in `server.ts` to provide deterministic responses when Gemini fails, preventing those pesky 502 errors. Finally, I\'ve shortened a sidebar label in `LayoutShell.tsx` and tightened up some spacing in `CustomerHomeView.tsx` as well.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "rcf-apLgIbrtkdUP9ZTjuAo"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_5773395210410682462"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Add graceful deterministic heuristic fallbacks with 200 OK on /api/ai/classify, /api/ai/search, and /api/ai/summarize when Gemini fails or is unavailable\", \"EndLine\":269, \"Instruction\":\"Return structured 200 heuristic fallback responses when Gemini throws or is unavailable so client workflows stay resilient with zero 502 errors\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"      const parsed = JSON.parse((response.text ?? \'{}\').trim());\\n      return res.json({ ...parsed, provider: \'gemini\' });\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      const msg = error instanceof Error ? error.message : \'AI classification unavailable\';\\n      console.warn(\'[AI Classify Fallback]\', msg);\\n      const { fileName = \'Document\', textSnippet = \'\' } = req.body as { fileName?: string; textSnippet?: string };\\n      const lower = `${fileName} ${textSnippet}`.toLowerCase();\\n      const category = lower.includes(\'resume\') || lower.includes(\'cv\')\\n        ? \'Resume\'\\n        : lower.includes(\'passport\') || lower.includes(\'aadhaar\') || lower.includes(\'id\')\\n        ? \'Identity\'\\n        : lower.includes(\'bank\') || lower.includes(\'invoice\') || lower.includes(\'receipt\')\\n        ? \'Banking\'\\n        : lower.includes(\'report\') || lower.includes(\'notes\') || lower.includes(\'semester\') || lower.includes(\'lab\')\\n        ? \'College\'\\n        : \'Personal\';\\n      const suggestedFolder =\\n        category === \'Resume\'\\n          ? \'Resumes & Career\'\\n          : category === \'Identity\'\\n          ? \'Identity & KYC\'\\n          : category === \'Banking\'\\n          ? \'Banking & Invoices\'\\n          : category === \'College\'\\n          ? \'Semester 7 Coursework\'\\n          : \'General Vault\';\\n      const cleanBase = fileName.replace(/\\\\.[^.]+$/, \'\').replace(/[_-]+/g, \' \').trim();\\n      return res.json({\\n        documentType: category,\\n        suggestedTitle: cleanBase || fileName,\\n        category,\\n        suggestedFolder,\\n        tags: [category.toLowerCase(), \'print-ready\', \'indexed\'],\\n        expiryDate: \'\',\\n        summary: `Indexed ${fileName} under ${category} for print preparation and quick search.`,\\n        ocrText: textSnippet || `Indexed document: ${cleanBase || fileName}. Ready for printing.`,\\n        recommendedColorMode: category === \'Identity\' || category === \'Resume\' ? \'color\' : \'bw\',\\n        recommendedSides: category === \'College\' ? \'double\' : \'single\',\\n        provider: \'heuristic\',\\n      });\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  // 3. AI Natural-Language Vault Search via Server-Side Gemini\\n  app.post(\'/api/ai/search\', async (req, res) => {\\n    try {\\n      const { query, documents } = req.body as {\\n        query?: string;\\n        documents?: Array<{\\n          id: string;\\n          name: string;\\n          category: string;\\n          tags: string[];\\n          ocrText: string;\\n          summary: string;\\n          createdAt: string;\\n        }>;\\n      };\\n\\n      if (!query || !Array.isArray(documents)) {\\n        return res.status(400).json({ error: \'query and documents array are required.\' });\\n      }\\n\\n      const ai = getGeminiClient();\\n      const catalog = documents.slice(0, 60).map((d) => ({\\n        id: d.id,\\n        name: d.name,\\n        category: d.category,\\n        tags: d.tags,\\n        summary: d.summary,\\n        ocrSnippet: (d.ocrText || \'\').slice(0, 300),\\n        createdAt: d.createdAt,\\n      }));\\n\\n      const response = await ai.models.generateContent({\\n        model: \'gemini-4-hydrogen\',\\n        contents: `User natural-language query: \\\"${query}\\\"\\\\n\\\\nVault documents:\\\\n${JSON.stringify(catalog)}`,\\n        config: {\\n          systemInstruction:\\n            \'You are a precise document search ranker. Return the IDs of matching documents ordered by relevance and a brief 1-sentence explanation.\',\\n          responseMimeType: \'application/json\',\\n          responseSchema: {\\n            type: Type.OBJECT,\\n            properties: {\\n              matchedIds: { type: Type.ARRAY, items: { type: Type.STRING } },\\n              explanation: { type: Type.STRING },\\n            },\\n          },\\n        },\\n      });\\n\\n      const parsed = JSON.parse((response.text ?? \'{\\\"matchedIds\\\":[],\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"\\\"}\').trim());\\n      return res.json({ ...parsed, provider: \'gemini\' });\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      const msg = error instanceof Error ? error.message : \'AI search unavailable\';\\n      console.warn(\'[AI Search Fallback]\', msg);\\n      const { query = \'\', documents = [] } = req.body as {\\n        query?: string;\\n        documents?: Array<{ id: string; name: string; category: string; tags?: string[]; ocrText?: string; summary?: string }>;\\n      };\\n      const tokens = query.toLowerCase().split(/\\\\s+/).filter((t) => t.length > 1);\\n      const matchedIds = documents\\n        .filter((d) => {\\n          const hay = `${d.name} ${d.category} ${(d.tags || []).join(\' \')} ${d.ocrText || \'\'} ${d.summary || \'\'}`.toLowerCase();\\n          return tokens.some((t) => hay.includes(t));\\n        })\\n        .map((d) => d.id);\\n      return res.json({\\n        matchedIds,\\n        explanation: `Matched ${matchedIds.length} document(s) locally across filenames, tags, and indexed text.`,\\n        provider: \'heuristic\',\\n      });\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  // 4. AI Document Summarizer & Smart Print Advisor\\n  app.post(\'/api/ai/summarize\', async (req, res) => {\\n    try {\\n      const { fileName, textContent, pageCount } = req.body as {\\n        fileName?: string;\\n        textContent?: string;\\n        pageCount?: number;\\n      };\\n      if (!fileName) {\\n        return res.status(400).json({ error: \'fileName is required.\' });\\n      }\\n\\n      const ai = getGeminiClient();\\n      const response = await ai.models.generateContent({\\n        model: \'gemini-4-hydrogen\',\\n        contents: `Document: ${fileName} (${pageCount || 1} pages)\\\\nContent:\\\\n${(textContent || \'No extracted text available.\').slice(0, 5000)}`,\\n        config: {\\n          systemInstruction:\\n            \'Summarize the document concisely in 2-3 sentences, list 3 key points, and suggest optimal print configuration (paper size, B&W vs color, single vs double-sided, binding).\',\\n          responseMimeType: \'application/json\',\\n          responseSchema: {\\n            type: Type.OBJECT,\\n            properties: {\\n              summary: { type: Type.STRING },\\n              keyPoints: { type: Type.ARRAY, items: { type: Type.STRING } },\\n              recommendedSettingsNote: { type: Type.STRING },\\n            },\\n          },\\n        },\\n      });\\n\\n      const parsed = JSON.parse((response.text ?? \'{}\').trim());\\n      return res.json({ ...parsed, provider: \'gemini\' });\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      const msg = error instanceof Error ? error.message : \'AI summarization unavailable\';\\n      console.warn(\'[AI Summarize Fallback]\', msg);\\n      const { fileName = \'Document\', pageCount = 1 } = req.body as { fileName?: string; pageCount?: number };\\n      const isLong = pageCount >= 8;\\n      return res.json({\\n        summary: `${fileName} (${pageCount} page${pageCount === 1 ? \'\' : \'s\'}) is prepared in your PrintReady vault.`,\\n        keyPoints: [\\n          `Detected ${pageCount} total page(s) ready for print layout.`,\\n          isLong ? \'Double-sided (duplex) printing will reduce paper usage by up to 50%.\' : \'Single-sided printing recommended for crisp presentation.\',\\n          \'Review page ranges and margin fit before final shop submission.\',\\n        ],\\n        recommendedSettingsNote: isLong\\n          ? \'Recommended: A4, B&W, Double-sided, Spiral Binding\'\\n          : \'Recommended: A4, Color or B&W, Single-sided, Standard 80gsm/100gsm\',\\n        provider: \'heuristic\',\\n      });\\n    }\\n  });\", \"StartLine\":164, \"TargetContent\":\"      const parsed = JSON.parse((response.text ?? \'{}\').trim());\\n      return res.json(parsed);\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      const msg = error instanceof Error ? error.message : \'AI classification failed.\';\\n      console.error(\'[AI Classify Error]\', msg);\\n      return res.status(502).json({ error: msg });\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  // 3. AI Natural-Language Vault Search via Server-Side Gemini\\n  app.post(\'/api/ai/search\', async (req, res) => {\\n    try {\\n      const { query, documents } = req.body as {\\n        query?: string;\\n        documents?: Array<{\\n          id: string;\\n          name: string;\\n          category: string;\\n          tags: string[];\\n          ocrText: string;\\n          summary: string;\\n          createdAt: string;\\n        }>;\\n      };\\n\\n      if (!query || !Array.isArray(documents)) {\\n        return res.status(400).json({ error: \'query and documents array are required.\' });\\n      }\\n\\n      const ai = getGeminiClient();\\n      const catalog = documents.slice(0, 60).map((d) => ({\\n        id: d.id,\\n        name: d.name,\\n        category: d.category,\\n        tags: d.tags,\\n        summary: d.summary,\\n        ocrSnippet: (d.ocrText || \'\').slice(0, 300),\\n        createdAt: d.createdAt,\\n      }));\\n\\n      const response = await ai.models.generateContent({\\n        model: \'gemini-4-hydrogen\',\\n        contents: `User natural-language query: \\\"${query}\\\"\\\\n\\\\nVault documents:\\\\n${JSON.stringify(catalog)}`,\\n        config: {\\n          systemInstruction:\\n            \'You are a precise document search ranker. Return the IDs of matching documents ordered by relevance and a brief 1-sentence explanation.\',\\n          responseMimeType: \'application/json\',\\n          responseSchema: {\\n            type: Type.OBJECT,\\n            properties: {\\n              matchedIds: { type: Type.ARRAY, items: { type: Type.STRING } },\\n              explanation: { type: Type.STRING },\\n            },\\n          },\\n        },\\n      });\\n\\n      const parsed = JSON.parse((response.text ?? \'{\\\"matchedIds\\\":[],\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"\\\"}\').trim());\\n      return res.json(parsed);\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      const msg = error instanceof Error ? error.message : \'AI search failed.\';\\n      console.error(\'[AI Search Error]\', msg);\\n      return res.status(502).json({ error: msg });\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  // 4. AI Document Summarizer & Smart Print Advisor\\n  app.post(\'/api/ai/summarize\', async (req, res) => {\\n    try {\\n      const { fileName, textContent, pageCount } = req.body as {\\n        fileName?: string;\\n        textContent?: string;\\n        pageCount?: number;\\n      };\\n      if (!fileName) {\\n        return res.status(400).json({ error: \'fileName is required.\' });\\n      }\\n\\n      const ai = getGeminiClient();\\n      const response = await ai.models.generateContent({\\n        model: \'gemini-4-hydrogen\',\\n        contents: `Document: ${fileName} (${pageCount || 1} pages)\\\\nContent:\\\\n${(textContent || \'No extracted text available.\').slice(0, 5000)}`,\\n        config: {\\n          systemInstruction:\\n            \'Summarize the document concisely in 2-3 sentences, list 3 key points, and suggest optimal print configuration (paper size, B&W vs color, single vs double-sided, binding).\',\\n          responseMimeType: \'application/json\',\\n          responseSchema: {\\n            type: Type.OBJECT,\\n            properties: {\\n              summary: { type: Type.STRING },\\n              keyPoints: { type: Type.ARRAY, items: { type: Type.STRING } },\\n              recommendedSettingsNote: { type: Type.STRING },\\n            },\\n          },\\n        },\\n      });\\n\\n      const parsed = JSON.parse((response.text ?? \'{}\').trim());\\n      return res.json(parsed);\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      const msg = error instanceof Error ? error.message : \'AI summarization failed.\';\\n      console.error(\'[AI Summarize Error]\', msg);\\n      return res.status(502).json({ error: msg });\\n    }\\n  });\", \"TargetFile\":\"/server.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Adding graceful AI fallbacks in server.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update server.ts AI fallbacks\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\310\020\n\305\020\001i\024}\023\243\r\031 \261\016U\206\f\3174\356\343\332y\345\017\374]\221\212\217\370\362T\353\253\226zO\301\377,\240\321Qx\230\t\337\375>\355\220\336D\221\325\207e<F\223\305m\361T\274\230eQh\363!\306c\234s\234\036n\247o\342\b\352\b4\020K=\031\210Z#\237va\330J\321x\032\213\204\357\304\222\\\234\233\\\022\350\250Um\276\306\021Y\266o)P`\336\220BY%DF\240\322\347\221G\377(%\315F\302\227=7\357T\276\262\306\313\034>`w\\\364,\377\341\036\246M\235\365|\376/\327z~\026\022x\231\273P\332n\004_H\352\t\252wM\257\363n\313\032\221\212V\302\313\222\267 \036_-J\355*\'\233\021\314J\345\204%O\371\232\233Y\213\327D\375e\001R\355\3027U.\320\207H\300>2nm\354\363\232>\316\3754$\355r:\201\245\035\274\350\027*\223\344\313_&\202(\377\351\34641\020\243\366[5.\f@\337\215t\r\234\326\224\316D\024\225\341\314\f1\360 \341t\362\316&q\240\332w@\365\030\n\005\216YLF\257\205Oj\322`_`U\004|5\261\f\376-\204\310\366\242\261NhDQ \206i@j\312{\313\026\253\276s\240W\026\031\245\252B9\333\b*\316aK\326F\347GG\364\320\a\301{\304`\025K\311\360jXV\333\223B\340\261\355\216Qqg\217\345\317\321\347\v_\205\346\252\341i\220ohz\0003\177\323\003\217 \275[u\354\274+\300R\245C\321<\306\320^`\3501\362q/\205l{%\rU@\366B6\304\231\223z\220\343\310\350Y\201V)\240\304\352N\304&G\345Ah\035\016\365w)HW.\250#\341\353(\356\320\213\203\346:\334\361\313\232\232\201\220O\345\226\267\214Y\331&\022\366\212\2543\302S\215\017\376\221\rN\\\351\336\362\b \325\335:h%_<\r\373t~@\321SF\204+\377\026r$\021P\024l^A\327\2620\027\200z\235:;\032g\341\221\023Ru\225\301\210G\371\346M\304\002\350H:\327\261\035\036\035\346\333\303w<\266\233_\246\a\373z\003\362\336L\331\277jG\365L\025\2241\351\327\237\244#\240\312\002\234t\346\343\216E\244B\023;\202\222\217X\f\0377mb\367\345Z<\337\264G\305\300\016\265RMKRW\263\207\255\376W&\032SP\366wb\346\232\023\034\321\r\205\351\207NbB\r\332\317m\374$\r\245\247y:\t\241\354L\017\366\n\273\304A\327\203\275\321\377\2566\243\327=\f\006\351j\255\206`j\314\312\314\037\251\337\217\301I\206\262\276\236\212Pd\217h\360\307\224\214\307=\025*gc\201\261M\346\207d,i{4K|\376\351-\270E\316\027w\327\264\326\252C\001$\025z\373\334\255eGW\205b:\312|SR\\\300\322&^\356\242\331#.\262\274\311\240\035\333\334)\265r\002|`\032\024=\356:\353\016/h\344\327 t\347\212\220W\006\306\237gR\r:Vp\322^\031\340\255\250I\270\234M\245VHbe\360\222,\325\367m\bb\036\016(Y\230Y\264\303us\245\006u\332\251\214\321\361\035\325\020\345\232r?w\017\037\263N\341>\362\001\357\334u\036\355\203\203\025\'\362\303\"E\024d\206/\370\276\034+)\\8\2028n\231d\313&\"\214\\\027\213\250ZJ\350\210\307\252\v\272\353\345\317\306\363\016YPsp\016M\327\317.\025\002?S?R\233\214\243\\n\224-\344\210\261N\020\255\362\035\233\357\002\032\340\334\2468X\254\211\027\240u\342r\242d\026kGK\276\330\247\215Q\001\277]j\277\262+\363\265\225Uk\006I\\\026\262\017,Nr!;\334Y\241\227R\3127\343\nt\004{\260\n\000J\351\302\233\025\312s\374L\017`\2342\017|\202\326\337\365\235\316k\200\021\017\352 \261\b~\017s\362@\225\342\232^\241Z\354i\t\253\327\022\272\a\236l\3333\202X\302\0029fl\350c\021\231\305\214\330\032~\310\316-\263\224\347\335\270\270\330\216\240\246\006\2525\344\247\345\307\326N\237\320_\302\352\205\221V\226e\024S\t>\325\337 \227\333O)\031\301=\a\026Q\353^\237aX\333\227/l\212\023xx.\035<e\250\324\312w\364\345\257\263X@}\364\244J\033\264\230\217\307\202r\314\243\005\260\216S\340\030\025\210\240_\2623>\346\2555\355\357\026\033\361\230\026;\236\005%Q\215.\206\357r?\334\033xKG\2133\301,\244h$2\230#\347\347\331QH[\274\341Z\017\2303\341w\203\a\026\331\363\n[\225\r\376\306r\037\231\325\224\225b;\247\327S/\244\216\330!\317\371=S\037\bbc\212\235\333f\020i?wXN\304\n{\237+\317\313\352\035\321\206\341\223\3003-?#yi\322\216K%\255Z_U\364S5:\272\253O&\364\367>\212\n\031\244R\214-Q\001\177\250\037L\245\241\233\255\234\315\261_\262\r%\346>Y,\306\337mj\340\363@\233?\373j\221\223\225O\306\217\377I\344\206N>\211P\027\245\302V[\"\240\3344\026;\355\204{\225Sm@\002\311\222\355\275\030<\301\326\262\271\361\246\202\024a\240\000\220\242\021E_\254\223s\307\302\343\326\207\233\022`\257\333\272\016\217\257\241X\341oQ\200r\320\360\n\300H\256\005P\356g\222\f\256wG\241X\256\204\2625\223O\360\004\264\205Gt\365\227\340\362\361O\032}\3667Eo\375 \217\332\245Y?\220L\312I\201\n\314,\024)u\213\002\332\203\377\323\343\325\'\323\255so\323\315:\300\263\265_\027\211\242=Gf\221\317\315\021F2#\b:\2773W\002\314(@\375\276I\3627o\267g\005m\262#\024\270\3536CC\242\211:\360\322B_\004S\336\2322_9\200\3426\020\301(\334\ra\303V\213\237\n\2541\360_\363\022[Wy\376\202\323!\375\030\227\375\177\221\366[\0312\017y:W!:\303J\221\340\341\331\250\223\361\314LEZ\371\2460\204\214\022\330]\207\311*O\240\275\222\350\262&\366/~\374\222\025 \354\250\277\334\201\247c:\363\373\241\221\211ka\375\n\003\0238%\340 \255\272\271\200w!\202\242\211\365\035\023\347-\262g\030\231{!B\272\243o\266cwDH\323/\321\231<\005\250N$\314\362\265\376|HVx\313\2574Q\265\250\274\377\370\v\032\362\314\220\313\247#\211\264\341\353Zs\210\225\210;\257\325\035Y\v\225QUT\017\363\216d\225g\267L\265v\251\\\211]\232\243\344h\262\371\361U\370\272b*_\361\304\350z\3729\262\244\264\332p\267(\241\f\224\215\374}3*d\0337\365\326\366+[`Xb\376ct?\373\267U\017\336\201\274\366\267\034\306\322i\212r\020\246\257\025\261@\230\276\236e\027\b\225\361\3454\260\a\266\252\3361Q#uTba\221&\020\a\367\244<P\250\336S\200\270\306\353?\311\326<}\030,4\336@Q\277\215H\314\r\205\352$\344&\021\236\2102\031\255=s\266\344\350\270\"\324\347oM\3564\344y\231\243\350\033\245\236\276\334\250\024\357\317\a{(Z\374dV\005\365\213\265\310\344\306rT\346.H\342c\326\vU\357?+D\020Fp\t`\242\252\f\301\352\256vc\r\177Lv\224\314+\231Z8\222\311\311T\'n~g\a\227J3\3537K\2423\244\'\030w\005\335F\031J\266\215\206\266\315\225\016%\016A>\032\221\254t\024\amC\311\a\227\"\020\327\002\257JG\n\236\344p\216\r\246\245\232\221t\373\000;\342\324\316\032\017\315\347Q\250~\"m\236\001\240\311B\243\275\266\215`\250\274P\370_\262\326\210\341\266)\320]\a8\337\000b\253|\330\343\254\371}\246{\201"
