Razorpay Test vs Live mode accurately.\n- `src/components/customer/CustomerOrdersView.tsx` \342\200\224 Wired the **Approve Price & Pay** modal to call `POST /api/create-order`, open the Razorpay Standard Checkout modal (`window.Razorpay`), handle modal dismissal (`modal.ondismiss`) and `payment.failed` events with inline alerts and toasts, and POST `{ razorpay_order_id, razorpay_payment_id, razorpay_signature }` to `POST /api/verify-payment` before marking the order as `Paid`.\n- `API_DOCUMENTATION.md` \342\200\224 Updated endpoint documentation for `/api/create-order` and `/api/verify-payment`.\n\n### 2. Verification Completed\n\n- **Unit Tests**: `11/11` passed (`src/domain/*.test.ts` and `server/razorpay.test.ts`), along with `npm run build` and `tsc --noEmit` (0 errors).\n- **Backend Endpoints Verified**:\n  - `POST /api/create-order` with `amount: 50` returned HTTP `400`.\n  - `POST /api/create-order` with `amount: 48000` created a live Razorpay test order (`order_U2025rq970iLCx`, HTTP `200`).\n  - `POST /api/verify-payment` returned HTTP `400` on missing fields and invalid signatures, and HTTP `200` (`verified: true`) on a valid HMAC-SHA256 signature.\n- **Browser & Secret Isolation Verified**:\n  - Verified `window.Razorpay` loads, clicking **Pay \342\202\271480.00 with Razorpay** creates a real order and opens the Razorpay Standard Checkout modal in Test Mode, and `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET` does not appear in source files or the client bundle.\n\n### 3. How to Test\n\n1. Start the server with `npm run dev` (already running on `http://localhost:3000`).\n2. Open **Customer Portal \342\206\222 Orders & Chat** and select order **`PR-2026-101`** (`\342\202\271480.00`, *Price Pending Approval*), or submit a new order from **Print Basket** and confirm its price from the **Shop** portal.\n3. Click **Approve Price & Pay**, then click **Pay \342\202\271480.00 with Razorpay**.\n4. In the Razorpay Test Mode checkout modal, complete a test payment (e.g., UPI `success@razorpay` or Razorpay\'s test NetBanking / Card flows), or close the modal to verify cancellation handling.\n5. Upon success, the frontend automatically sends `razorpay_order_id`, `razorpay_payment_id`, and `razorpay_signature` to `/api/verify-payment`, verifies the signature on the server, and transitions the order to **Paid** with the Razorpay payment ID.\n\n### 4. Manual Steps Required for Production\n\n- Replace the `rzp_test_*` credentials in your production environment secrets with live `RAZORPAY_KEY_ID`, `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET`, and `VITE_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID` keys before accepting real payments.\n- Optionally configure `RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET` and point Razorpay Dashboard webhooks to `/api/payments/webhook` for asynchronous settlement notifications."
