  planner_response {
    response: "**No \342\200\224 do not paste live or sensitive secrets in chat.**\n\n### Where to add them safely instead\n1. **In AI Studio**: Open the **Secrets / Environment Variables** panel in the AI Studio UI and add the variable names from `.env.example` (`RAZORPAY_KEY_ID`, `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET`, `VITE_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID`, `RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, etc.). They are injected securely at runtime without entering chat history or source code.\n2. **When running locally or deploying**: Add them directly into your local `.env` file (already ignored by `.gitignore`) or your hosting provider\'s secret manager.\n\n### Note on the keys already configured\n- Your current `.env` uses **Razorpay Test Mode** keys (`rzp_test_*`), which only simulate payments and cannot move real money. You can still regenerate them anytime in **Razorpay Dashboard \342\206\222 Account & Settings \342\206\222 API Keys**.\n- When switching to **Live Mode** (`rzp_live_*`), always set `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET` strictly through the Secrets panel / server environment \342\200\224 never in chat and never prefixed with `VITE_`."
    thinking: "**Prioritizing Safety Protocols**\n\nI\'ve established a firm rule: under no circumstances should live secrets be pasted in the chat. This includes sensitive data like API keys, passwords, and tokens. It\'s a fundamental principle of security that I\'ve cemented. My focus is on keeping this information secure.\n\n\n**Clarifying Secret Handling**\n\nI\'m now detailing where sensitive credentials belong: definitely not in chat. AI Studio Build\'s Secrets panel or local `.env` files are ideal locations, avoiding chat history. I\'m also addressing the test keys shared earlier, confirming their safety for testing purposes, but emphasizing the need for Live Mode keys when deploying.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "k9H-auWoAYLg_uMP6fSb6QQ"
    modified_response: "**No \342\200\224 do not paste live or sensitive secrets in chat.**\n\n### Where to add them safely instead\n1. **In AI Studio**: Open the **Secrets / Environment Variables** panel in the AI Studio UI and add the variable names from `.env.example` (`RAZORPAY_KEY_ID`, `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET`, `VITE_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID`, `RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, etc.). They are injected securely at runtime without entering chat history or source code.\n2. **When running locally or deploying**: Add them directly into your local `.env` file (already ignored by `.gitignore`) or your hosting provider\'s secret manager.\n\n### Note on the keys already configured\n- Your current `.env` uses **Razorpay Test Mode** keys (`rzp_test_*`), which only simulate payments and cannot move real money. You can still regenerate them anytime in **Razorpay Dashboard \342\206\222 Account & Settings \342\206\222 API Keys**.\n- When switching to **Live Mode** (`rzp_live_*`), always set `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET` strictly through the Secrets panel / server environment \342\200\224 never in chat and never prefixed with `VITE_`."
