  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering User\'s Needs**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the essence of \"build app for customer.\" PrintReady\'s current setup, a unified 3-portal workspace with a clear Workspace switcher (`Customer` | `Shop` | `Admin`) in the sidebar, feels strong for internal demos. This design may be a useful starting point for something customer-facing, but more thinking is needed for the specific use case.\n\n\n**Refining Customer-Centric Design**\n\nI\'ve realized the PrintReady demo\'s internal focus on a unified workspace is a liability for external use. I\'m prioritizing a streamlined customer experience. The goal is a mobile-ready app with a clean interface. Core features will include Home, Document Vault, Scanner & PDF Tools, Print Basket, Print Shops, and Orders. The design is now focused on a consumer-grade experience, without any Admin/Shop distractions.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Mobile Navigation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the mobile experience, which feels paramount. I\'m moving toward a mobile-first design with a bottom navigation bar, for quick access to core functions like Home, Vault, Scan, Basket, and Orders. The design will be hidden on larger screens, to keep a consistent UI. Customer Account/Shop Partner/Admin are hidden by design, unless specifically needed.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "wNL-auT3N_f8nsEP3oK2qQU"
