  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing a Customer App**\n\nI\'m focusing now on a customer-first design for the PrintReady app. I\'m imagining a dedicated, installable application with a clean, consumer-friendly interface. The goal is to provide a seamless experience, removing all admin clutter from the user\'s view. I\'m exploring how to achieve clear, easy navigation within the app\'s structure.\n\n\n**Refining Navigation & Access**\n\nI\'m currently revising the app\'s navigation and access points. I\'m removing the external integration matrix from customer settings, replacing it with an \"Install App & Support\" section. I\'m also adding buttons to open the shop owner portal or the admin console, keeping the customer interface simple and friendly, including clear navigation using query parameters and a responsive back button.\n\n\n**Implementing Mobile Navigation**\n\nI\'m now implementing a fixed bottom navigation bar for mobile users, including \"Home,\" \"Vault,\" \"Scan,\" \"Basket\" with a live count, and \"Orders\" with an active count. I\'m focusing on providing safe-area bottom padding to ensure a native app feel. I\'m also ensuring that \"Print Shops\" and \"Account & Security\" are easily accessible through the header and mobile drawer. This is a critical step in streamlining the mobile experience.\n\n**Building Progressive Web App**\n\nI\'m now focusing on making a Progressive Web App (PWA). I\'ve installed `vite-plugin-pwa` as a dev dependency and am generating the necessary PNG icons in the `/public/` directory (including `pwa-192x192.png`, `pwa-512x512.png`, `pwa-maskable-512x512.png`, and `apple-touch-icon.png`). I\'m planning to use a Node canvas script or SVG-to-PNG via Playwright/sharp for crisp, vector-rendered PNGs. Next, I\'ll configure `VitePWA` in `/vite.config.ts`.\n\n\n**Configuring PWA Manifest**\n\nI\'m now integrating the PWA manifest. I\'ve set the name to `\'PrintReady\'`, with `start_url: \'/\'`, `scope: \'/\'`, `display: \'standalone\'`, and colors to match the brand. I am also working on configuring Workbox caching to exclude the `/api/*` route. I will also incorporate appropriate additions to my configuration and HTML files as well. I\'m updating my `tsconfig.json` and `index.html` to be correctly updated for PWA functionality. I\'m focused now on developing PWA installation components.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "5dL-aqHTOO2QxN8PrO_d4A8"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_8489475752525330966"
      name: "install_applet_package"
      arguments_json: "{\"IsDevDependency\":true, \"PackageNames\":[\"vite-plugin-pwa\"], \"toolAction\":\"Installing vite-plugin-pwa for customer PWA\", \"toolSummary\":\"Install vite-plugin-pwa\"}"
