  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Executing PWA Updates**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! `run-code` works in an ESM context, meaning I can bypass `require` and directly use inline SVG strings. This opens the door to generating those crisp PNG icons. I plan to tackle parallelizing the customer app and PWA updates soon, and I\'m currently reviewing the files I will update.\n\n\n**Implementing PWA Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating the VitePWA plugin into `/vite.config.ts`, ensuring a complete manifest with details like name, start URL, and display options. I\'m carefully configuring Workbox caching, excluding `/api/` from the navigation fallback, and keeping the existing asset copying plugin intact. I\'m also updating `/tsconfig.json` and `/index.html` with PWA and iOS Safari meta tags, including the apple-touch-icon. Further, I am updating the necessary context files.\n\n\n**Refining Portal Navigation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the portal navigation. I\'m updating `LayoutShell.tsx` to handle different portals accessed via URL query parameters, with \"customer\" as the default. I\'m removing the workspace switcher, and adding a \"Back to Customer App\" link for non-customer portals. The sidebar footer will be updated, and I\'m mounting the PWA install button in the header. Plus, a mobile bottom navigation bar is in progress.\n\n\n"
