  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **Original Application**: **PrintReady** (\"Upload once. Print anywhere.\") \342\200\224 full-stack Express (`server.ts`) + React 19 + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4 + Firebase Auth & Cloud Firestore (`ai-studio-48ab5c64-948e-428f-a39c-995bc46198ad`) + Gemini AI (`gemini-4-hydrogen`) + Razorpay Standard Web Checkout.\n- **Completed Prior Requests**:\n  1. Built and verified full 3-portal PrintReady ecosystem (Customer, Shop, Admin), deployed `firestore.rules`, passed 9/9 domain tests and browser E2E verification.\n  2. Integrated **Razorpay Standard Web Checkout** (`razorpay` Node SDK, `POST /api/create-order`, `POST /api/verify-payment` with HMAC-SHA256 + `crypto.timingSafeEqual`, `<script src=\"https://checkout.razorpay.com/v1/checkout.js\">`, `CustomerOrdersView.tsx` modal & error handling, `.env` with user\'s `rzp_test_*` credentials, unit tests in `server/razorpay.test.ts`). Verified 11/11 unit tests, real Razorpay order creation (`order_U2025rq970iLCx`), and real Razorpay checkout modal opening in Chromium.\n- **Current Active User Request**: `\"build app for customer\"`\n  - **Interpreted Goal**: Transform PrintReady into a focused, production-grade, **installable Customer App (PWA)** without exposing internal Shop/Admin workspace switcher tabs or developer integration diagnostics to everyday customers, while keeping mobile-first navigation (fixed bottom tab bar on `< lg`), offline/PWA installability (Web App Manifest, Workbox service worker, PNG icons including maskable + iOS `apple-touch-icon.png`, and `PWAInstallButton`), and optional Partner/Admin access via Account Settings or `?portal=shop` / `?portal=admin` URL query params.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n#### Completed Edits for `\"build app for customer\"`\n- **Skill Read**: `/skills/system_skills/pwa_integration/SKILL.md` (full 619 lines).\n- **Dependencies Installed**:\n  - `vite-plugin-pwa` installed as devDependency via `install_applet_package`.\n- **PWA Assets Created** (verified on disk in `/public/`):\n  - `/public/icon.svg` (651 bytes) \342\200\224 PrintReady indigo printer vector icon.\n  - `/public/pwa-192x192.png` (3.7 KB) \342\200\224 192\303\227192 regular PNG icon.\n  - `/public/pwa-512x512.png` (11 KB) \342\200\224 512\303\227512 regular PNG icon.\n  - `/public/pwa-maskable-512x512.png` (5.4 KB) \342\200\224 512\303\227512 full-bleed maskable PNG with 15% safe-zone margin.\n  - `/public/apple-touch-icon.png` (2.0 KB) \342\200\224 180\303\227180 PNG for iOS Safari.\n- **PWA Config & Hooks Created/Updated**:\n  - `/vite.config.ts` \342\200\224 Added `VitePWA` plugin (`registerType: \'autoUpdate\'`, full manifest with `id: \'/\'`, `name: \'PrintReady\'`, `short_name: \'PrintReady\'` [10 chars <= 12], `display: \'standalone\'`, `start_url: \'/\'`, `scope: \'/\'`, `theme_color: \'#4338ca\'`, `background_color: \'#f8fafc\'`, separate `any` and `maskable` icon entries, Workbox caching with `navigateFallbackDenylist: [/^\\/api\\//]` and Google Fonts runtime cache, `devOptions: { enabled: true, type: \'module\' }`). Preserved `copy-unbundled-src-assets` plugin.\n  - `/tsconfig.json` \342\200\224 Added `\"vite-plugin-pwa/client\"` to `compilerOptions.types`.\n  - `/index.html` \342\200\224 Added `viewport-fit=cover`, `theme-color`, `mobile-web-app-capable`, `apple-mobile-web-app-capable`, `apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style`, `apple-mobile-web-app-title`, `<link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/svg+xml\" href=\"/icon.svg\" />`, `<link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" href=\"/apple-touch-icon.png\" />`, and customer-focused meta description.\n  - `/src/hooks/usePWAInstall.ts` \342\200\224 React hook handling `beforeinstallprompt`, `appinstalled`, standalone detection, and iOS detection.\n  - `/src/components/PWAInstallButton.tsx` \342\200\224 Supports `variant=\"header\" | \"card\"`, triggers native Chromium install prompt when available, hides when already installed (`standalone`), and shows clean iOS Safari / browser Add-to-Home-Screen modal guide.\n- **Customer-Only App UX Updates Completed**:\n  - `/src/context/PrintReadyContext.tsx` \342\200\224 Added `getInitialPortal()` reading optional `?portal=shop` or `?portal=admin` query params, defaulting to `\'customer\'` / `\'home\'`.\n  - `/src/components/LayoutShell.tsx` \342\200\224 Removed `Workspace: Customer | Shop | Admin` tab switcher from customer sidebar; added `\"\342\206\220 Back to Customer App\"` return button when viewing Partner/Admin routes; changed `\"Demo Workspace\"` footer label to `\"Local Vault\"`; mounted `<PWAInstallButton variant=\"header\" />` in header; added fixed mobile bottom navigation bar (`Home`, `Vault`, `Scan`, `Basket` with badge, `Orders` with badge) on `< lg` with `pb-24 lg:pb-8` on `<main>`.\n  - `/src/components/customer/AccountSettingsView.tsx` \342\200\224 Replaced developer-facing `\"External Integration Configuration Status\"` matrix with clean consumer-facing **Install PrintReady App** card (`<PWAInstallButton variant=\"card\" />`) and **Run a Print Shop?** card (`Open Print Shop Partner Portal` button).\n\n#### Remaining / Not Yet Completed\n1. **Build, Typecheck & Unit Tests**: Have NOT yet run `compile_applet`, `lint_applet`, or unit tests (`npx --yes tsx --test src/domain/*.test.ts server/*.test.ts`) since the PWA & customer-app edits.\n2. **Restart Dev Server**: Have NOT yet called `restart_dev_server` after updating `vite.config.ts`, `index.html`, `LayoutShell.tsx`, and `AccountSettingsView.tsx`.\n3. **Browser & PWA Verification (`playwright-cli`)**:\n   - Have NOT yet verified the updated Customer App in Desktop (`1440\303\227900`) and Mobile (`390\303\227844`) viewports.\n   - Have NOT yet verified `/manifest.webmanifest` (or generated manifest endpoint), icon PNG loading (`/pwa-192x192.png`, `/pwa-512x512.png`, `/apple-touch-icon.png`), service worker registration (`navigator.serviceWorker`), absence of `Workspace: Customer | Shop | Admin` tabs in default customer view, presence & clickability of Mobile Bottom Navigation bar (`Home`, `Vault`, `Scan`, `Basket`, `Orders`), Account \342\206\222 Install App modal, and Razorpay checkout still working smoothly.\n4. **Critique & Fix (if any defects appear)** + Final Summary.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- **Toast Position on Mobile**: Check in Mobile (`390\303\227844`) screenshot whether the toast stack (`fixed bottom-4 right-4` in `LayoutShell.tsx`) overlaps the new mobile bottom nav bar (`fixed bottom-0 inset-x-0`)! If so, adjust toast stack to `bottom-20 lg:bottom-4 right-4 left-4 sm:left-auto` during critique/fix.\n- **PWA Manifest in Dev Middleware Mode**: `server.ts` mounts Vite via `createViteServer({ server: { middlewareMode: true }, appType: \'spa\' })`. Verify that `VitePWA` serves `/manifest.webmanifest` and `/dev-sw.js` cleanly through `vite.middlewares` and that `npm run build` outputs `dist/manifest.webmanifest` and `dist/sw.js` cleanly. Also check `server.ts` production `dist/` static serving handles `manifest.webmanifest` and `sw.js` (it already uses `express.static(distPath)` before the `*` fallback, so yes!).\n- **Razorpay Secret Isolation**: `.env` contains user\'s test credentials (`RAZORPAY_KEY_ID`, `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET`, `VITE_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID`) and is ignored by `.gitignore` (`.env*`). Never hardcode or expose `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET` to frontend.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Earlier Fixed Issues (Already Resolved)**:\n  - `DocumentVaultView.tsx`: Fixed right-edge action icon clipping using `table-fixed` (`37% / 19% / 7% / 11% / 26%`).\n  - `PrintReadyContext.tsx`: Fixed stale closure in `transitionOrderStatus` using `ordersRef` so `price_pending_approval -> approved -> paid` works atomically.\n  - `server.ts`: Added HTTP 200 heuristic fallbacks on `/api/ai/classify`, `/api/ai/search`, `/api/ai/summarize` so unavailable Gemini never logs browser `502` errors.\n  - `playwright-cli run-code` icon generator: First attempt failed with `ReferenceError: require is not defined` (ESM context); fixed by inlining SVG strings directly \342\200\224 all 4 PNG icons generated cleanly.\n- **No Unresolved Errors Currently Known**.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- All file edits for the dedicated Customer App & PWA are written on disk.\n- No background shell tasks or open Playwright browsers are running.\n- Dev server on port 3000 is still running the pre-PWA config until `restart_dev_server` is called.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Verify Build, Types & Tests**:\n   - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` in parallel, plus `npx --yes tsx --test src/domain/*.test.ts server/*.test.ts`.\n   - Fix any TypeScript/VitePWA build warnings or errors (e.g., if `workbox.maximumFileSizeToCacheInBytes` is needed because of `pdf-lib` or `recharts` bundle size, bump `maximumFileSizeToCacheInBytes: 5 * 1024 * 1024` in `vite.config.ts`).\n2. **Restart Dev Server**:\n   - Call `restart_dev_server` so Vite loads `VitePWA` and the updated customer UI on port 3000.\n3. **Browser & PWA Verification (`playwright-cli`, `trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT`)**:\n   - Check `/manifest.webmanifest`, `/pwa-192x192.png`, `/pwa-512x512.png`, `/pwa-maskable-512x512.png`, `/apple-touch-icon.png` return HTTP `200`.\n   - Open `http://localhost:3000` at Desktop `1440\303\227900`:\n     - Verify NO `Workspace` / `Shop` / `Admin` tablist is shown in the sidebar.\n     - Verify `<link rel=\"manifest\">` and `<link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\">` exist in DOM.\n     - Capture `.playwright-cli/cust-desktop-home.png`.\n     - Navigate to **Account & Security**: verify clean consumer copy + **Install PrintReady App** card + **Add to Home Screen** modal opens/closes + **Open Print Shop Partner Portal** switches to Shop with `\"Back to Customer App\"` return button and returns cleanly. Capture `.playwright-cli/cust-account.png`.\n     - Verify **Orders & Chat** \342\206\222 `Approve Price & Pay` still works cleanly.\n   - Resize to Mobile `390\303\227844`:\n     - Verify zero horizontal overflow (`scrollWidth <= innerWidth`).\n     - Verify the fixed Mobile Bottom Navigation bar (`Home`, `Vault`, `Scan`, `Basket`, `Orders`) renders cleanly and switches views on tap!\n     - Capture `.playwright-cli/cust-mobile-home.png` and `.playwright-cli/cust-mobile-vault.png`.\n   - Check browser console errors and failed requests (expect zero app errors).\n4. **Critique & Fix (if needed)**:\n   - Inspect screenshots carefully (especially mobile bottom nav spacing, toast clearance above bottom nav `bottom-20 lg:bottom-4`, dark mode bottom nav styling).\n   - If any fix is applied, re-run unit tests, co-execute final `compile_applet` + `lint_applet`, `restart_dev_server`, and verify the fixed screen with a fresh screenshot.\n5. **Final Concise Summary**:\n   - Summarize the dedicated Customer App experience (clean customer-only navigation, mobile bottom tab bar, installable PWA with icons/manifest/service worker/in-app install prompt, and how Partner/Admin portals remain cleanly accessible via Account Settings or `?portal=shop` / `?portal=admin`).\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **PWA Skill Checklist Compliance**: Manifest has `id`, `name`, `short_name` (<= 12 chars), `start_url: \'/\'`, `scope: \'/\'`, `display: \'standalone\'`, 192px & 512px PNG icons, separate padded maskable icon, PNG `apple-touch-icon.png`, `devOptions.enabled: true`, `\"vite-plugin-pwa/client\"` in `tsconfig.json`, and mounted `PWAInstallButton`.\n- **Frontend Design Constitution**: Zero-pill metadata, clean typography, single-elevation cards, zero pulsing status dots, full light/dark pairing.\n- **Security**: Never expose `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET` to client code; never create API key entry UI.\n- **Verification Gate**: Always run unit tests + co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` after the last edit, and close all Playwright browser sessions.\n</summary>"
