  planner_response {
    response: "PrintReady is now built as a dedicated, installable **Customer App (PWA)**.\n\n### What Changed\n- **Customer-Only Navigation**: Removed the internal `Workspace (Customer / Shop / Admin)` switcher from the sidebar so customers only see consumer features (**Home**, **Document Vault**, **Scanner & PDF Tools**, **Print Basket**, **Print Shops**, **Orders & Chat**, and **Account & Security**).\n- **Mobile-First App Shell**: Added a fixed bottom navigation bar on mobile (`Home`, `Vault`, `Scan`, `Basket`, `Orders`) with live item/order badges, iOS safe-area padding, and lifted toast notifications so nothing overlaps the tab bar.\n- **Installable PWA & Offline Support**: Configured a Web App Manifest, Workbox service worker, full icon set (192\303\227192, 512\303\227512, maskable 512\303\227512, and 180\303\227180 iOS `apple-touch-icon`), and an in-app **Install App / Add to Home Screen** prompt that triggers native installation on supported browsers or shows step-by-step instructions on iOS Safari.\n- **Consumer-Ready Account Settings**: Replaced the developer integration diagnostics panel with an **Install PrintReady App** card and a **Run a Print Shop?** card.\n- **Partner & Admin Access**: Print shop partners can still open their workspace from **Account & Security \342\206\222 Open Print Shop Partner Portal** (or directly via `?portal=shop` and `?portal=admin`), with a **Back to Customer App** button in the sidebar.\n\n### Verification\n- Verified production build (`vite build` + Workbox service worker and manifest generation), TypeScript check (`tsc --noEmit`), and all 11 unit tests.\n- Verified desktop (`1440\303\227900`) and mobile (`390\303\227844`) views, PWA manifest/icon endpoints, bottom tab navigation, install guide modal, and Razorpay checkout flow with zero console errors or horizontal overflow."
    thinking: "**Verifying Successful Build**\n\nEverything looks good! I\'ve confirmed a successful build, with all 11 unit tests passing and no errors reported in compilation or linting. The build process generated the manifest, service worker, and all necessary PNG icons. Full build verification is complete.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "9dT-aoGMKJSGxs0Phb2_mA8"
    modified_response: "PrintReady is now built as a dedicated, installable **Customer App (PWA)**.\n\n### What Changed\n- **Customer-Only Navigation**: Removed the internal `Workspace (Customer / Shop / Admin)` switcher from the sidebar so customers only see consumer features (**Home**, **Document Vault**, **Scanner & PDF Tools**, **Print Basket**, **Print Shops**, **Orders & Chat**, and **Account & Security**).\n- **Mobile-First App Shell**: Added a fixed bottom navigation bar on mobile (`Home`, `Vault`, `Scan`, `Basket`, `Orders`) with live item/order badges, iOS safe-area padding, and lifted toast notifications so nothing overlaps the tab bar.\n- **Installable PWA & Offline Support**: Configured a Web App Manifest, Workbox service worker, full icon set (192\303\227192, 512\303\227512, maskable 512\303\227512, and 180\303\227180 iOS `apple-touch-icon`), and an in-app **Install App / Add to Home Screen** prompt that triggers native installation on supported browsers or shows step-by-step instructions on iOS Safari.\n- **Consumer-Ready Account Settings**: Replaced the developer integration diagnostics panel with an **Install PrintReady App** card and a **Run a Print Shop?** card.\n- **Partner & Admin Access**: Print shop partners can still open their workspace from **Account & Security \342\206\222 Open Print Shop Partner Portal** (or directly via `?portal=shop` and `?portal=admin`), with a **Back to Customer App** button in the sidebar.\n\n### Verification\n- Verified production build (`vite build` + Workbox service worker and manifest generation), TypeScript check (`tsc --noEmit`), and all 11 unit tests.\n- Verified desktop (`1440\303\227900`) and mobile (`390\303\227844`) views, PWA manifest/icon endpoints, bottom tab navigation, install guide modal, and Razorpay checkout flow with zero console errors or horizontal overflow."
