  planner_response {
    response: "**Customers never see or enter any of these.** That screen is **your app owner Secrets panel** in AI Studio\342\200\224it automatically lists every variable defined in `.env.example`.\n\n### Why they showed up (and which ones you actually need)\n\n1. **Actually needed (only 2 for payments):**\n   - `RAZORPAY_KEY_ID` and `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET` \342\200\224 Required on the server so your app can create Razorpay orders and verify payments when a customer clicks **Approve Price & Pay**.\n   - (`GEMINI_API_KEY` and `APP_URL` are already managed automatically by AI Studio.)\n\n2. **Not required at all (can be left blank or removed):**\n   - **`VITE_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID`** \342\200\224 Optional fallback; the backend already sends the public `key_id` from `RAZORPAY_KEY_ID` when creating an order.\n   - **`RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET`** \342\200\224 Only needed if you later configure background Razorpay webhooks; checkout already verifies signatures immediately via `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET`.\n   - **`EMAIL_SMTP_HOST / USER / PASS / FROM_ADDRESS`** \342\200\224 Unused placeholder for future automated server emails. Right now, customers send documents via their own email app (`mailto:`), which needs no SMTP setup.\n   - **`WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN / PHONE_NUMBER_ID`** \342\200\224 Unused placeholder for the paid WhatsApp Business Cloud API. Right now, WhatsApp sharing opens directly in the customer\'s WhatsApp (`wa.me`), which needs no API keys.\n\nWould you like me to remove those unused optional variables from `.env.example` so your Secrets panel only shows what the app genuinely needs?"
    thinking: "**Discovering Hidden Insights**\n\nI\'ve just made a significant discovery! Grep revealed that customers never interact with or input data into the \"Secrets Panel.\" That section within the screenshot is exclusively for the app owner or developer.\n\n\n**Analyzing Secret Configurations**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the AI Studio configuration, specifically focusing on secret keys. I\'ve realized that the `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `APP_URL` are auto-injected. The only necessary secrets for Razorpay Standard Checkout are `RAZORPAY_KEY_ID` and `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET`. Interestingly, `VITE_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID` is not strictly required. The `RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is also optional, only necessary for webhook registration. SMTP configurations will be analyzed next.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "g9X-apq9J7Poz7IP2POeoA4"
    modified_response: "**Customers never see or enter any of these.** That screen is **your app owner Secrets panel** in AI Studio\342\200\224it automatically lists every variable defined in `.env.example`.\n\n### Why they showed up (and which ones you actually need)\n\n1. **Actually needed (only 2 for payments):**\n   - `RAZORPAY_KEY_ID` and `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET` \342\200\224 Required on the server so your app can create Razorpay orders and verify payments when a customer clicks **Approve Price & Pay**.\n   - (`GEMINI_API_KEY` and `APP_URL` are already managed automatically by AI Studio.)\n\n2. **Not required at all (can be left blank or removed):**\n   - **`VITE_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID`** \342\200\224 Optional fallback; the backend already sends the public `key_id` from `RAZORPAY_KEY_ID` when creating an order.\n   - **`RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET`** \342\200\224 Only needed if you later configure background Razorpay webhooks; checkout already verifies signatures immediately via `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET`.\n   - **`EMAIL_SMTP_HOST / USER / PASS / FROM_ADDRESS`** \342\200\224 Unused placeholder for future automated server emails. Right now, customers send documents via their own email app (`mailto:`), which needs no SMTP setup.\n   - **`WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN / PHONE_NUMBER_ID`** \342\200\224 Unused placeholder for the paid WhatsApp Business Cloud API. Right now, WhatsApp sharing opens directly in the customer\'s WhatsApp (`wa.me`), which needs no API keys.\n\nWould you like me to remove those unused optional variables from `.env.example` so your Secrets panel only shows what the app genuinely needs?"
