    thinking: "**Refining The Vision**\n\nI am now focusing on creating a *pure* customer-facing app. My priority is absolute cleanliness: specifically removing any unnecessary secrets from the `.env.example` file. This means stripping out all Razorpay, SMTP, and WhatsApp Cloud API keys to avoid any accidental exposure. The goal is a *customer-only* print-ready app, entirely free of sensitive information.\n\n\n**Eliminating Payment Systems**\n\nI\'m systematically removing all traces of payment integration. This involves deleting specific files like `razorpay.ts`, as well as purging payment-related code from the server, including API routes, and front-end components. I\'ve also removed the Razorpay script from the HTML and updated the `CustomerOrdersView.tsx` to remove the payment flow entirely. My focus is now on direct payment options within the app.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Customer Features**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on customer-centric features, eliminating shop and admin portals entirely. I am focusing on prominent \"Open in WhatsApp\" and \"Send via Email\" buttons right on every print request, along with direct payment. The goal is a clean, streamlined customer experience, and I\'m pruning the code to reflect this shift. I am removing shop and admin-related code.\n\n\n**Prioritizing User Actions**\n\nI\'m removing the \"Run a Print Shop?\" and \"Open Print Shop Partner Portal\" options and only maintaining the \"**Install PrintReady App**\" card. The card will be presented alongside \"**Quick Share Defaults**\" to give the user quick access to sharing info for Whatsapp and email. Additionally, I am simplifying the `PrintReadyContext.tsx` by always setting the portal to \'customer\'. I\'m also going to prioritize the WhatsApp and Email redirect, making them top-level actions within `PrintBasketView.tsx`. Customers will now have the ability to select from saved, nearby, or custom print shops to share print settings.\n\n\n**Enhancing Sharing Options**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the user\'s sharing experience for print requests, which will include pre-filled print specifications. This involves integrating direct WhatsApp and email redirects to streamline communication. I will also incorporate a \"Save Print Request\" feature and a \"Customize Message & Templates\" modal. Furthermore, I will include WhatsApp and email redirect buttons on shop cards in Discover and Saved lists, and in shop profile drawers. This will streamline the printing process for the end-user.\n\n\n"
