  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visuals: Basket**\n\nI\'m currently captivated by the \"cust-only-basket.png\" screenshot. I\'m focusing on the \"Send Print Job\" option in the right panel. It\'s a straightforward idea for redirecting users to WhatsApp or Email, with pre-filled print specifications, and it seems like it will be very user-friendly. I\'m assessing how well this solution addresses the user\'s needs for direct print job submission.\n\n\n**Exploring Print Options**\n\nI\'ve been examining the print request details and action bar from the \"cust-only-requests.png\" screenshot. I\'ve noted the \'Send via WhatsApp\' and \'Send via Email\' options, but now I\'m seeing \"Confirm Estimate\" and \"Cancel Request\", too. I\'m excited by the \'Pay Directly at the Shop\' focus, and the ability to save requests. I like the simplified interface without Razorpay, and I\'m looking closely at how the subtotal works.\n\n\n**Clarifying Cost Breakdown**\n\nI\'m now diving into the calculations in `PrintBasketView.tsx` and realizing we need to make the cost breakdown crystal clear for direct shop payments. The goal is to avoid any customer confusion. So I\'m proposing a change to display the \"Estimated Shop Cost\" as the \"Printing & Finishing Subtotal\" minus any discount, plus delivery fee. This directly reflects the actual shop cost and eliminates any perceived hidden fees. I\'m also considering highlighting the transparency with a formula.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "Mdj-apruCZaG28oPyqGiaQ"
