  planner_response {
    response: "PrintReady is now a **customer-only app** with **no payment integration** and direct **WhatsApp and Email redirect options**.\n\n### What Changed\n- **Customer-Only App**: Removed the Shop Partner Portal and Admin Console completely from routing, navigation, and Account Settings. Customers only see **Home**, **Document Vault**, **Scanner & PDF Tools**, **Print Basket**, **Print Shops**, **Print Requests**, and **Account & Security**.\n- **Payment Integration Removed**: Removed Razorpay (`checkout.razorpay.com`, SDK dependency, backend `/api/create-order` / `/api/verify-payment` / `/api/payments/webhook` endpoints, and payment modals). Print estimates are shown for reference and customers settle directly at the shop on pickup or delivery.\n- **Zero Extra Secrets Required**: Cleaned `.env.example` down to only the standard `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `APP_URL` variables\342\200\224no Razorpay, SMTP, or WhatsApp Cloud API secrets are needed.\n- **Direct WhatsApp & Email Redirect Everywhere**:\n  - **Print Basket**: Primary **Send via WhatsApp** (`https://wa.me/...`) and **Send via Email** (`mailto:...`) buttons pre-fill the shop recipient, document list, copies, paper size, color/sides, binding, pickup/delivery details, and estimated cost\342\200\224plus a **Custom WhatsApp / Email...** option for any local print shop.\n  - **Print Shops**: One-tap WhatsApp and Email redirect buttons directly on every shop card and inside each shop\'s profile drawer.\n  - **Print Requests**: One-tap **Send on WhatsApp** and **Send via Email** redirect actions pre-filled with the request number, files, settings, and pickup code.\n\n### Verification\n- Verified production build (`vite build` + PWA manifest/service worker), TypeScript check (`tsc --noEmit`), and all 9 domain unit tests.\n- Verified in Chromium on Desktop (`1440\303\227900`) and Mobile (`390\303\227844`) that `?portal=shop` stays in the Customer App, WhatsApp and Email redirect URLs build accurately for both saved and custom shops, no Razorpay or payment UI remains, and there are zero console errors or horizontal overflows."
    message_id: "eNj-av2SAfSwvdIPkv6z2AY"
    modified_response: "PrintReady is now a **customer-only app** with **no payment integration** and direct **WhatsApp and Email redirect options**.\n\n### What Changed\n- **Customer-Only App**: Removed the Shop Partner Portal and Admin Console completely from routing, navigation, and Account Settings. Customers only see **Home**, **Document Vault**, **Scanner & PDF Tools**, **Print Basket**, **Print Shops**, **Print Requests**, and **Account & Security**.\n- **Payment Integration Removed**: Removed Razorpay (`checkout.razorpay.com`, SDK dependency, backend `/api/create-order` / `/api/verify-payment` / `/api/payments/webhook` endpoints, and payment modals). Print estimates are shown for reference and customers settle directly at the shop on pickup or delivery.\n- **Zero Extra Secrets Required**: Cleaned `.env.example` down to only the standard `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `APP_URL` variables\342\200\224no Razorpay, SMTP, or WhatsApp Cloud API secrets are needed.\n- **Direct WhatsApp & Email Redirect Everywhere**:\n  - **Print Basket**: Primary **Send via WhatsApp** (`https://wa.me/...`) and **Send via Email** (`mailto:...`) buttons pre-fill the shop recipient, document list, copies, paper size, color/sides, binding, pickup/delivery details, and estimated cost\342\200\224plus a **Custom WhatsApp / Email...** option for any local print shop.\n  - **Print Shops**: One-tap WhatsApp and Email redirect buttons directly on every shop card and inside each shop\'s profile drawer.\n  - **Print Requests**: One-tap **Send on WhatsApp** and **Send via Email** redirect actions pre-filled with the request number, files, settings, and pickup code.\n\n### Verification\n- Verified production build (`vite build` + PWA manifest/service worker), TypeScript check (`tsc --noEmit`), and all 9 domain unit tests.\n- Verified in Chromium on Desktop (`1440\303\227900`) and Mobile (`390\303\227844`) that `?portal=shop` stays in the Customer App, WhatsApp and Email redirect URLs build accurately for both saved and custom shops, no Razorpay or payment UI remains, and there are zero console errors or horizontal overflows."
