  planner_response {
    response: "It is a **Web App** configured as an **Installable Progressive Web App (PWA)** \342\200\224 not a native Android (`.apk`) or iOS (`.ipa`) store app.\n\n### What that means in practice\n- **Works immediately via URL**: Customers can open it directly in Chrome, Safari, or Edge on mobile and desktop without downloading from an app store.\n- **Installs like an app on phones**: Because PWA support is configured (manifest, service worker, and app icons), customers can tap **Install App** (Android/Chrome) or **Share \342\206\222 Add to Home Screen** (iPhone/Safari) to put a **PrintReady** icon on their home screen and launch it full-screen with offline caching and a mobile bottom tab bar.\n- **Limitations compared to a native app**: It is not published on the Google Play Store or Apple App Store out of the box, and WhatsApp/Email sharing redirects to the user\'s WhatsApp or Email app with the text pre-filled (the user still attaches the file and taps Send inside WhatsApp/Email).\n\n### If you want a Play Store / App Store native app later\n- **Fastest path (keep this codebase)**: Wrap this PWA into an Android/iOS package using **Capacitor** or **PWABuilder / Bubblewrap (TWA)** to publish on the Play Store or App Store.\n- **Fully native path**: Build a dedicated mobile app in **Kotlin (Android)**, **Swift (iOS)**, **Flutter**, or **React Native**."
    thinking: "**Clarifying The Application Type**\n\nI\'ve determined the answer is straightforward. I\'ll respond directly: it\'s a web app designed as an installable Progressive Web App (PWA). This explanation should be very clear and easy to understand.\n\n\n"
